/* ═══ Persian calendar occasions — generated, do not edit by hand ═══
   Written by scripts/build-occasions.mjs from the public Iranian calendar data
   transcribed from time.ir:

     https://raw.githubusercontent.com/drarahimi/persian-holidays/main/api/v1/<gregorian-year>/shamsi.json
     https://raw.githubusercontent.com/samanzamani/PersianHoliday/main/persian_holiday.db
     (the database is read only for the 2 years past the JSON export)

   Solar only. The official Solar Hijri calendar and Iran's own occasions are
   what this app is for, so the lunar (Hijri) occasions — the religious days that
   move every year — are left out at build time. A page of them would have had to
   keep a per-year table growing forever, and it would answer a question the
   reader did not ask this calendar. A handful of national dates whose names
   mention a religious figure (Imam Khomeini's passing, 14 Khordad…) are solar,
   fixed, and stay.

   Structure:
     TITLES — every occasion name once; the rows below point into it.
     FIXED  — [month, day, titleId, holiday] solar occasions, the same Jalali
              day every year. Carried for years outside RANGE.
     YEARS  — { jalali year: { 'month-day': [[titleId, holiday], …] } }.
     RANGE  — the Jalali years YEARS covers.

   Generated: 2026-11-13 */

